\title{ensannot: Ensembl gene annotation without biomaRt}
\description{
Builds a local, reusable gene annotation table straight from the Ensembl FTP
site (the core MySQL dump files, read as plain tab-delimited text, so no SQL
server or SQL knowledge is needed) and uses it to annotate your own tables.
}
\section{Workflow}{

\strong{Part 1 - build once, reuse forever}
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=ens_build_annotation]{ens_build_annotation()}} downloads, parses and caches the table for one
species / release / assembly.
\item \code{\link[=ens_load_annotation]{ens_load_annotation()}} reloads a cached object (or a saved file).
\item \code{\link[=ens_list_cached]{ens_list_cached()}} shows what is cached.
\item \code{\link[=ens_resolve_db_url]{ens_resolve_db_url()}} turns species, assembly and release into the FTP folder.
}
\strong{Part 2 - annotate your data}
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=ens_annotate_ids]{ens_annotate_ids()}}: details for Ensembl gene IDs.
\item \code{\link[=ens_annotate_regions]{ens_annotate_regions()}}: all genes overlapping each region (returns a
per-region table and a gene table).
\item \code{\link[=ens_annotate_loci]{ens_annotate_loci()}}: genes overlapping each locus, or the closest
genes within a distance.
}
\code{\link[=ens_example_annotation]{ens_example_annotation()}} returns a tiny synthetic annotation so every
example in this package runs offline.
